{"name":"Bloodthirsty Warlock","hex":"#ec1837","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodthirsty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Thirsty for blood: inexorably violent or eager for bloodshed; murderous.","Of a book, film, etc.: depicting much violence; gory, violent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodthirsty"},{"term":"warlock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male magic-user; a male equivalent of a witch; a wizard.","A magic-user (regardless of gender)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warlock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bloodthirsty","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodthirsty is a 1970s Japanese vampire film trilogy produced by Toho Studio, consisting of three of their 1970s horror films: The Vampire Doll, Lake of Dracula and Evil of Dracula. While there is no plot connection between the films, they share a vampire theme. The films were all directed by Michio Yamamoto and co-written by Ei Ogawa."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodthirsty"},{"title":"Warlock","blocks":[{"text":"A warlock is traditionally a male practitioner of witchcraft or sorcery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Warlocks_and_Witches_in_a_dance._John_Faed_RSA._1855.jpg/330px-Warlocks_and_Witches_in_a_dance._John_Faed_RSA._1855.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warlock"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Mefistofele_warlock.jpg/330px-Mefistofele_warlock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Mefistofele_warlock.jpg/330px-Mefistofele_warlock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Costume design for a warlock for the opera Mefistofele (Alfredo Leonardo Edel, 1881)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMefi